WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.290
Picture a footballer paid 50,000 a week.

2
00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:05.510
His best other job would be coaching,

3
00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:07.730
which would pay 2,000 a week.

4
00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:10.160
Cut his pay by thousands
and he would still

5
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:12.240
play rather than coach.

6
00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.090
If a star would happily play for far less,

7
00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:17.190
why are they paid so much?

8
00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:20.300
In this mission, you'll
split a wage into two parts,

9
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.010
using a supply curve.

10
00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:24.680
Then you'll use a graph
lab to rotate the supply

11
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:27.790
curve and watch the two parts change size.

12
00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:30.480
Your mission: find out
why someone who would work

13
00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.410
for far less is still paid so much.
